93596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193595 #edb/ref 1061 40678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193595 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5f6b707c-1a02-5a01-96da-00e64ed94944" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193595 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186193857 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193596 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193596 #edb/ref 1061 40680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193596 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8bd1113e-49e3-508c-a22f-dfa0fdd69bae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193596 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193616 #edb/ref 1061 41154 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193616 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7f037845-d12e-5297-90be-1612950af662" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193616 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193673 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193674 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193673 #edb/ref 1061 42013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193673 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0ed50c81-73e4-55ef-8062-730a3a7ba23a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193673 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193674 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193674 #edb/ref 1061 42014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193674 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "75c54c3c-1feb-55cc-a726-bb26875bb42a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193674 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193857 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we have a pair of parallel lines cut by a transversal.\n\n**Alternate interior angles** are the pairs of angles on *alternate* (opposite) sides of the transversal and are *interior* to (inside of) the parallel lines. These pairs of angles always have equal measure.\n\n![](images/b0/b06ff1e3d55ee09f95a1234ab4aa340d825f05971957ae8a88ff408c256c82a4.png)\n\n**Alternate external angles** are the pairs of angles on *alternate* (opposite) sides of the transversal and are *exterior* to (outside of) the parallel lines. These pairs of angles always have equal measure.\n\n![](images/4d/4d4765d2f5e49794336d2bf35705da9fa7885ce0a619dcd3a117d28cfe66645e.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193857 #edb/ref 1065 6723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193857 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "17eba692-165e-58c9-96a3-8aed2c660530" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193857 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510770 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186511635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510770 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510770 #edb/ref 1045 "Lines and Angles in Circles" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510770 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186511635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510770 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "c5317150-479c-5e7c-86c3-dd80600c2591" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510903 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510903 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510903 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "35f29ca2-0fa4-5b57-89ea-772c55ec32c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510929 #edb/ref 1080 "180-10x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510929 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510929 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3f80b711-19ed-52be-8297-190fa8f36a8c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510960 #edb/ref 1080 "45" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510960 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510960 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "527947cd-9a5e-5103-893d-eef7754c5992" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511094 #edb/ref 1080 "5x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511094 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511094 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "964ae523-a001-56a9-918a-6ed65ac952c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511109 #edb/ref 1080 "110" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511109 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511109 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9c4e7a13-93c7-5102-ac8c-81