80 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511422 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ca229fee-40f1-5f93-90d7-5d892f402841" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511429 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186511094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511429 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511429 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511429 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186511094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511429 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d30ec5d2-7185-5122-ad13-5d37e66f9e20" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511434 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186511170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511434 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511434 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511434 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186511170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511434 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "deda8d33-afb6-5faa-bc94-281563101948" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511436 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186510929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511436 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511436 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511436 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186510929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511436 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e17cb2f5-7c1b-57d6-8e9f-2a843b07d5bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511452 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511452 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048764 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511452 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049027 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511452 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049223 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511452 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049376 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511452 #edb/ref 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049856 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511452 #edb/ref 1089 #edb/ref 17592186511454 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511452 #edb/ref 1090 #uuid "c0924dd4-d44b-56a7-9578-fec2204b0185" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511454 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186511610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511454 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186511637 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511454 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186511650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511454 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186511664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511454 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186511669 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511454 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186511671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511454 #edb/ref 1085 "![](images/23/2364a0b3b1f379c1b091528ffeed46caafad8db153d63979e36ab9cc6b0a6c9d.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $O$ is the center of the circle, $∠AOD$ and $∠BOE$ are straight angles, $m∠BOC={(5x+5)}^{∘},$ and $m∠DOE={(5x-5)}^{∘}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511454 #edb/ref 1086 #uuid "2da1acf2-080b-52d3-9b85-82ed9d0b8cb2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511454 #edb/ref 1087 #edb/ref 17592186511664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511516 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511516 #edb/ref 1069 "q-142517" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511516 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511516 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/72/72c697336f9518e5be1c8b89d9244c0952a7b8f5e77f007638e6a9405d98d8fd.png)\n\nFind an expression in terms of $x$ for the measure of $∠ODC.$\n\n$m∠ODC=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511516 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "839696c7-ab7c-5fbc-a053-f39b3696e2a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511516 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $\\overset{―}{OC}$ and $\\overset{―}{OD}$ are radii of the circle, the triangle $△OCD$ is isosceles. Consequently, the base angles must have the same measure:\n\n$$\n∠OCD=∠ODC.\n$$\n\nAlso, from step 3, we know that $m∠COD={(180-10x)}^{∘}.$\n\n![](images/50/509c6fd7ffabd5c4f7b71e89dd94cb29c374dd6d2d64407d65bcdef44553c60e.png)\n\nNow, since the internal angles of any triangle sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠ODC+m∠OCD+m∠COD & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠ODC+(m∠ODC)+(180-10x)^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2m∠ODC-10{x}^{∘} & ={0}^{∘} \\\\ 2m∠ODC & =10{x}^{∘} \\\\ m∠ODC & =5{x}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $m∠ODC=5{x}^{∘}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511531 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511436 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511531 #edb/ref 1069 "q-142504" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511531 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511531 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/f3/f3f38ca1b55a12dcaffc5a52eb4f08fc6d6ec3d5c746cb8215ad3e0ed7671153.png)\n\nFind an expression in terms of $x$ for the measure of $∠COD.$\n\n$m∠COD=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511531 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "99fbfa91-9f2d-531e-9a33-54900502faa9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511531 #edb/ref 1074 "We're given that $∠BOE$ is a straight angle, so\n\n$$\nm∠BOE={180}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNow, the angle addition postulate gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠BOC+m∠COD+m∠DOE & =m∠BOE \\\\ (5x+5)^{∘}+m∠COD+(5x-5)^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 10{x}^{∘}+m∠COD & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠COD & =(180-10x)^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511550 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511345 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511550 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511550 #edb/ref 1069 "q-142519" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511550 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511550 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/82/828ac748b9d8c87e4a7a66dfddb2e926a3362830d551653260b5974b6bd2ca1a.png)\n\nGiven that the line segments $\\overset{―}{CD}$ and $\\overset{―}{AF}$ are parallel and $m∠FAO={(3x+18)}^{∘},$ find the measures of $∠FAO$ and $∠AOE.$\n\n$∠FAO=$\n{{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}$\n\n$∠AOE=$\n{{field-2}}\n${}^{∘}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511550 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c18e889b-e4ac-54b0-ba7c-c7c1982b19f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511550 #edb/ref 1074 "The parallel line segments $\\overset{―}{CD}∥\\overset{―}{AF}$ are cut by the transversal $\\overset{―}{AD}.$\n\nThe angles $∠ODC$ and $∠FAO$ are interior to the parallel line segments and are on opposite sides of the transversal. So, they are alternate interior angles and consequently, they have the same measure.\n\nIn step 4, we found that $m∠ODC=5{x}^{∘}.$\n\nSetting the measures of $∠ODC$ and $∠FAO$ equal to each other, we have an equation that we can solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠ODC & =m∠FAO \\\\ 5{x}^{∘} & =(3x+18)^{∘} \\\\ 5x & =3x+18 \\\\ 2x & =18 \\\\ x & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $x=9$ into the expressions for the measures of $∠FAO$ and $∠AOE$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠FAO & =(3x+18)^{∘} \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 9+18)^{∘} \\\\  & ={45}^{∘} \\\\ m∠AOE & =(185-5x)^{∘} \\\\  & =(185-5\\cdot 9)^{∘} \\\\  & ={140}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $m∠FAO={45}^{∘}$ and $m∠AOE={140}^{∘}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511551 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511551 #edb/ref 1069 "q-142509" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511551 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511551 #edb/ref 1071 "If $AD=8,$ then $OC=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511551 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c19df22d-0aea-5f35-9eda-6b27f1f826b3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511551 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that the points $A,C,$ and $D$ lie on the circle. We know that the radius of the circle is $r=OC.$\n\nWe first notice that\n\n$$\nAD=AO+OD.\n$$\n\nNow, $\\overset{―}{AO}$ and $\\overset{―}{OD}$ are both segments between the center of the circle and the circle itself. So, they are both radii of the circle, and because $AD=8,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AD & =8 \\\\ AO+OD & =8 \\\\ r+r & =8 \\\\ 2r & =8 \\\\ r & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nOC=r=4.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511552 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511552 #edb/ref 1069 "q-142529" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511552 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511552 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/96/96a76584c5ddbcc39d221334803c6791cb3b459178e70c310e4eca54a4e85462.png)\n\nFind an expression in terms of $x$ for the measure of the angle $∠AOE.$\n\n$∠AOE=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511552 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c3360eb5-04da-59fb-81da-119f0aeb047a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511552 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $∠AOD$ is a straight angle, the angles $∠AOE$ and $∠DOE$ are supplementary. Two angles are supplementary if their measures add up to ${180}^{∘}.$ \n\nSo, the measure of the angle $∠AOE$ that's supplementary to the angle of $∠DOE=5x-{5}^{∘}$ must be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠AOE & ={180}^{∘}-(5x-5)^{∘} \\\\  & =({180}^{∘}+{5}^{∘})-5{x}^{∘} \\\\  & ={(185-5x)}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511562 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511371 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511562 #edb/ref 1069 "q-142717" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511562 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511562 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/4b/4ba93d3eb8944d086b001c0aa01cb28251705a6af9e55a9fd58e2affce12acaa.png)\n\nIn the quadrilateral $AOEF,$ the angle $∠E$ measures ${65}^{∘}.$ Then, $m∠F=${{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511562 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "db1a27df-5d87-50c3-9b60-42007a434557" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511562 #edb/ref 1074 "A quadrilateral has $n=4$ sides, so the sum of its interior angles must be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2) & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot (4-2) \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom step 5, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & =m∠FAO={45}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠O & =m∠AOE={140}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/f6/f67441e3999a8b81e7ac63555c729f0f6c31bff015477efc3031364c6fb22003.png)\n\nAdding up the interior angles, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A+m∠O+m∠E+m∠F & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {45}^{∘}+{140}^{∘}+{65}^{∘}+m∠F & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {250}^{∘}+m∠F & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ m∠F & ={110}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $m∠F={110}^{∘}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511610 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186511637 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511610 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "36e26965-83de-5b3a-a837-f8ef84516946" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511610 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186511551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511635 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8497e842-c3b2-58b8-aae2-6d721a1570af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511635 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186511452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511637 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186511669 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511637 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "867555f1-c71e-5f0b-92e3-462ed0c033fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511637 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186511531 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511650 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "aa8ca3fb-cd47-59bb-82d0-c65e6c47f3c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511650 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186511562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511664 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186511610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511664 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ce50a472-77e1-5d95-aaa6-ceb0722f1141" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511664 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186511552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511669 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186511671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511669 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d96f6e55-4607-5688-9493-18aef8f0e341" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511669 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186511516 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511671 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186511650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511671 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e0458b15-e3cd-5149-8fd1-535fa754ff89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511671 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186511550 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
